## Astronomical Calculation

The astronomical calculation use skyfield to interpolate. We choose de406 to cover the range 3000 BC - 3000 AD.





## Horizon Adjustment

The 2016 paper does not take into account that stars set in the west, and Mt Olympus of Lesbos is to the west of Myteline. So the horizon is higher, and the Pleiades would set earlier.

    def horizon_adjust(from_location,to_location) -> Float:
